            <div xml:id="d329">

                <pb facs="0376" n="364" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg364"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.91/3–645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-06T16:00:00+03:25">March 6, 1945—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 6—3:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>154. Foreign Minister Entezam, who seemed much worried, told me last night that
                    Molotov in his latest interview with Iranian Ambassador Ahy, had pointedly
                    renewed Soviet complaint against asserted anti-Russian attitude of Iranian
                    Government. Molotov made special reference to law forbidding oil concessions and
                    said Soviets were holding it against Iran. This interview was subsequent to
                    Yalta Conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
